 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   The mask $M$ must correctly identify pixels containing content in the reprojected images to avoid comparing against empty or background regions [S1].
-*   The method relies on the differentiability of the point-based reprojection process [S1].
+*   The mask $M$ must accurately exclude background regions to prevent the photo-consistency loss from penalizing empty pixels [S1].
+*   The method requires the reprojection pipeline to be fully differentiable with respect to the input image colors [S1].
